 "note": "P13's oracle: the buffer decode of chapter 13 step 6, the drop count of step 7 and the fill-to-drain ratio of step 8. Every decode expectation is integer arithmetic, written by hand from the field layout and checked against the implementation before being emitted, so no decode case passes on a tolerance. The field positions are a stated layout and not a claim about the part: the chapter gives only the word shape, a tag byte and six data bytes, and sends the tag format to each sensor's datasheet. Every finding here holds for any counter field narrower than a byte. The budget cases are floating point and are compared to a relative 1e-12.",
